  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#37859\", \"PowerToys#47648\", \"PowerToys#46873\"], \"answer\": \"This crash has been reported before. PowerToys#37859 is the main tracking ticket, and the others were closed as duplicates of it. The stack trace is the same as yours: a NullReferenceException in BindingExpression.SetupDefaultValueConverter, thrown from ThemeManager.OnSystemThemeChanged. It happens when WPF re-applies the Windows theme. In the earlier reports this followed waking from sleep or hibernate, unlocking the PC, or a monitor or dock change. One reporter said it may be linked to a tool that switches between light and dark mode automatically after wake-up (PowerToys#45219). The earlier crashes were mostly one-off. The archive has no confirmed fix, so I can't point you to one. After a crash, restart PowerToys and it should keep working. Please add any steps that reliably trigger it to PowerToys#37859, such as sleep, wake, a theme change or a monitor change. Please also say whether you use an automatic theme switcher.\"}",
